1.1 Security Control Types and Categories
1.1	Compare and contrast various types of Security Controls
-	Control types can fit into multiple categories based on context


Security Control Definition
Security measures for countering and minimizing loss or unavailability of services or apps due to vulnerabilities. The terms safeguards and countermeasures may seem to be used interchangeably. Safeguards are proactive (reduce likelihood of occurrence). Countermeasures are reactive (reduce impact after occurrence)
