Control Types:
Deterrent
-	Deployed to discourage violation of security policies.
Preventive
-	Deployed to thwart or stop unwanted or unauthorized activity from occurring.
Detective
-	Deployed to discover or detect unwanted or unauthorized activity.
Compensating
-	Provides options to other existing controls to aid in enforcement of security policies.
Corrective
-	Modifies the environment to return systems to normal after an unwanted or unauthorized activity has occurred.
Directive
-	Direct, confine, or control the actions of subjects to force or encourage compliance with security policies.

